<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Japonisme</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Japonisme was the fashion for Japanese art and design in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and America in the later nineteenth century, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> opened to the West. Japanese woodblock prints influenced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/impressionism">Impressionism</a>, Post-Impressionism and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/art-nouveau">Art Nouveau</a>. The site presents it as part of the cultural legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>.</p></div>
